    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0248" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 185.161/1: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps">George Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>,” <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-05T21:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 5, 1918—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your Dec. 5, 11 a.m. Matter attended to.</p>
                <p>President replied to an inquiry by Gompers as to the holding of an International
                    Labor Conference that he saw no objection to its being held. He added ‘that he
                    thought it advisable for Gompers to be present at Paris in any event.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
